      "side": 1,
      "message": "PS3 scope is right — dropping `content:review` removes the change-edit overlap.\n\nThe core ref-update path is sound: the new commit is always parented on the current branch tip. Nice test coverage, too.\n\n-1 for one more PS. Details are in the inline comments, several with apply-able suggestions; by theme:\n\n* Blocking: REST verb/name (`ProjectRestApiModule`) — maintainer input please, before the URL freezes; silently-dropped rename/delete ops in mixed batches (`CommitFileModifications`) → 400.\n* Fixes: `validation_options` threading (`CommitFilesInput` + `BranchCommitBuilder` ×2); `file_mode` on delete/rename → 400; gitlink `160000` scope (`CommitFilesInput` + doc table); doc contract — atomicity, commit identity, not-a-push, `base_revision` CAS wording; six boundary tests + a Java-API test (`PutContentIT`, suggestion verified locally).\n* Discuss: require `commit_message` vs keep the `Update files` default (`BranchCommitBuilder`).\n\nTwo points with no file to own them:\n\n1. Signed push: this endpoint never sees a push certificate, so a signed-push requirement on the ref is silently bypassed. Exempt (document) or enforce (gate)? Maintainer call.\n2. Size limits: `receive.maxObjectSizeLimit` is receive-pack-only (`AsyncReceiveCommits` → `ReceivePack.setMaxObjectSizeLimit`); this endpoint inserts via a plain `ObjectInserter`. Same bypass as change edits / create-change, so not a regression — I\u0027d accept and document, unless you want push parity.",
