      "message": "`content` already means one file\u0027s bytes at `FILE_KIND` (L65). This branch-scoped batch commit isn\u0027t that — and it creates a new commit on every call, so it\u0027s an action, not an idempotent PUT of a resource. I\u0027d use `post(BRANCH_KIND, \"commit\")`, matching the POST convention for actions (`rebase`, `submit`, `cherrypick`); if a symmetric single-file write is wanted later, `put(FILE_KIND, \"content\")` can be added separately.\n\nWould be good to hear what other maintainers think about the naming here before the URL freezes.",
